%description:

Tcp.accEcnOptionEnabled:on -- the ACK of the handshake comes with the AccECN option.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "AccECN: send the AccECN option, which gives the byte counts of each ECN
codepoint (RFC 9768 section 3.2.3.3: RECOMMENDED); false: only the ACE field (Linux
tcp_ecn_option=0). Each connection reads it at its open".

The classes: on (true, the default), off (false), and changed (the value changes during the
run; the parameter is @mutable). The code: TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() reads it at
the open; the AccECN option goes on the SYN-ACK, on the ACK of the handshake and on the first
data segment of the client, and later after a byte count changed (TcpConnection::writeHeaderOptions()). This test separates "on" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, an AccECN client (tcpEcnMode "accecn"; host2 "accecn-passive":
preconditions). A header of 32 bytes has the Timestamps option only; the AccECN option adds 12
bytes. Observation: level 1, the ACK of host1 at the end of the handshake comes with the AccECN option.

%# parameter: Tcp.accEcnOptionEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.accEcnOptionEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAccEcnOptionEnabledOn")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackBit == true && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.headerLength > 32B")
             .describe("the ACK of the handshake of host1")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAccEcnOptionEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.accEcnOptionEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn-passive"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAccEcnOptionEnabledOn: PASS
